  "body": "## What changed\n\nRequested in #225: \"Spindle speed should be editable under the Feeds tab, and should be settable from rpm or surface speed.\"\n\n- The Feeds tab's **Cutting data** group gets an editable **Spindle speed** row (new `egui_app/spindle_row.rs`) with an **rpm / surface** switch - surface speed in m/min in a millimetre document, SFM in an inch one, through the tool's diameter (Vc = pi D n).\n- The speed lives on the op's tool (`Tool::rpm` - what the post writes as S), so a committed value is **one undoable `ChangeTool`**: a draft rides egui's temp memory while the field is held, and the commit lands on drag release, Enter or focus loss - never a command per frame. The row's hover says it edits the tool for every operation using it, the same law the tool-material and flutes rows beside it keep. A zero/negative/non-finite speed is refused by name on the status line.\n- The switch is view state (`State::spindle_as_vc`).\n- Not done: a per-operation spindle override (a schema + post change - its own issue if wanted). Decision recorded in `RECOMMENDED.md` (#225).\n\n## Gate (own worktree build, current main)\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-ui`: every binary green except the lib's `egui_shell_snapshot_light` (Diff 1) and `tool_editor_snapshot` (Diff 4) - software-GL diffs with the same counts on main on this machine. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean (second commit).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::spindle_row::tests::surface_speed_and_rpm_invert_in_both_units` (100 m/min on a 10 mm cutter; 130.9 SFM for 1/2\" at 1000 rpm; round trips)\n- `egui_app::spindle_row::tests::a_new_speed_is_one_change_tool_and_a_same_or_bad_one_is_none`\n- `egui_app::tests::spindle_row::the_feeds_tab_offers_the_spindle_speed_and_its_unit_switch`\n\nChangelog: Spindle speed is editable on the Feeds tab, as rpm or surface speed (m/min / SFM)\n\nOutside contributor PR (fork) - feat, merges at the next cut.\n\nFixes #225\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
